sn46.54:4.6 | P: iti uddhamadho tiriyaṁ sabbadhi sabbattatāya sabbāvantaṁ lokaṁ upekkhāsahagatena cetasā vipulena mahaggatena appamāṇena averena abyāpajjena pharitvā viharathā’ti. | T: equanimity … without ill will.’
sn46.54:4.7 | S: What, then, is the difference between the ascetic Gotama’s teaching and instruction and ours?” | T: So, friends, what here is the distinction, the disparity, the difference between the ascetic Gotama and us, that is, regarding the one Dhamma teaching and the other, regarding the one manner of instruction and the other?”
sn46.54:5.1 | S: Those mendicants neither approved nor rejected that statement of the wanderers of other religions. | T: Then those bhikkhus neither delighted in nor rejected the statement of those wanderers.
